,"Senior Researcher",false,"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=OvKEnVwAAAAJ&hl=en","https://images.deepai.org/author-profile/remi-munos-thumb-1602.jpg",5,"Has made foundational contributions to reinforcement learning theory and policy optimization; he speaks to the workshop's core questions around optimization dynamics and the theoretical underpinnings of preference-based update rules.","src/content/speakers/remi-munos.md","00c4d23300c15e14",{"html":26,"metadata":27},"\u003Cp>Has made foundational contributions to reinforcement learning theory and policy optimization; he speaks to the workshop’s core questions around optimization dynamics and the theoretical underpinnings of preference-based update rules.\u003C/p>",{"headings":28,"localImagePaths":29,"remoteImagePaths":30,"frontmatter":31,"imagePaths":32},[],[],[],{"name":14,"affiliation":15,"talkTitle":16,"role":17,"url":19,"photo":20,"order":21},[],"remi-munos.md","yali-du",{"id":34,"data":36,"body":45,"filePath":46,"digest":47,"rendered":48,"legacyId":56},{"name":37,"affiliation":38,"talkTitle":39,"role":40,"confirmed":41,"url":42,"photo":43,"order":44},"Yali Du","King's College London","WIP","Associate Professor",true,"https://yalidu.github.io","https://yalidu.github.io/images/yalidu.png",2,"Works on reinforcement learning and multi-agent systems; her research on reward design and learning under uncertainty contributes to the workshop's interest in preference feedback modeling and adaptive data collection.","src/content/speakers/yali-du.md","d9f8c9272a64c48e",{"html":49,"metadata":50},"\u003Cp>Works on reinforcement learning and multi-agent systems; her research on reward design and learning under uncertainty contributes to the workshop’s interest in preference feedback modeling and adaptive data collection.\u003C/p>",{"headings":51,"localImagePaths":52,"remoteImagePaths":53,"frontmatter":54,"imagePaths":55},[],[],[],{"name":37,"affiliation":38,"talkTitle":39,"role":40,"confirmed":41,"url":42,"photo":43,"order":44},[],"yali-du.md","ramponi",{"id":57,"data":59,"body":66,"filePath":67,"digest":68,"rendered":69,"legacyId":77},{"name":60,"affiliation":61,"talkTitle":39,"role":62,"confirmed":41,"url":63,"photo":64,"order":65},"Giorgia Ramponi","University of Zurich","Assistant Professor","https://sites.google.com/view/alpi-lab/giorgia-ramponi?authuser=0","https://www.ifi.uzh.ch/contacts/ifi/alpi/gramponi/photo/gionew.jpeg.jpeg",3,"Works on safe and robust reinforcement learning in non-stationary settings; her research connects directly to the workshop's emphasis on robustness, feedback loops, and safety-relevant failure modes under task evolution.","src/content/speakers/ramponi.md","11fd4bc8c2469e69",{"html":70,"metadata":71},"\u003Cp>Works on safe and robust reinforcement learning in non-stationary settings; her research connects directly to the workshop’s emphasis on robustness, feedback loops, and safety-relevant failure modes under task evolution.\u003C/p>",{"headings":72,"localImagePaths":73,"remoteImagePaths":74,"frontmatter":75,"imagePaths":76},[],[],[],{"name":60,"affiliation":61,"talkTitle":39,"role":62,"confirmed":41,"url":63,"photo":64,"order":65},[],"ramponi.md","van-der-schaar",{"id":78,"data":80,"body":87,"filePath":88,"digest":89,"rendered":90,"legacyId":98},{"name":81,"affiliation":82,"talkTitle":39,"role":83,"confirmed":41,"url":84,"photo":85,"order":86},"Mihaela van der Schaar","University of Cambridge","John Humphrey Plummer Professor","https://www.vanderschaar-lab.com/prof-mihaela-van-der-schaar/","https://www.vanderschaar-lab.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/mihaela-2023-1.png",1,"Known for her work on machine learning for dynamic, real-world decision-making; she contributes perspectives on adaptive methods, uncertainty quantification, and principled evaluation, key themes around post-training under changing conditions.","src/content/speakers/van-der-schaar.md","a8e9b3e2d92e0444",{"html":91,"metadata":92},"\u003Cp>Known for her work on machine learning for dynamic, real-world decision-making; she contributes perspectives on adaptive methods, uncertainty quantification, and principled evaluation, key themes around post-training under changing conditions.\u003C/p>",{"headings":93,"localImagePaths":94,"remoteImagePaths":95,"frontmatter":96,"imagePaths":97},[],[],[],{"name":81,"affiliation":82,"talkTitle":39,"role":83,"confirmed":41,"url":84,"photo":85,"order":86},[],"van-der-schaar.md","rachel-bawden",{"id":99,"data":101,"body":108,"filePath":109,"digest":110,"rendered":111,"legacyId":119},{"name":102,"affiliation":103,"talkTitle":16,"role":104,"confirmed":18,"url":105,"photo":106,"order":107},"Rachel Bawden","INRIA","Principal Investigator","https://rbawden.github.io","https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1653912785529-613a0c85e63aa832a98cecc4.png",4,"Works on natural language processing and computational linguistics; she brings expertise in how language models handle shifting linguistic contexts, directly relevant to the workshop's focus on evolving task definitions and evaluation criteria.","src/content/speakers/rachel-bawden.md","27a90518c6c07bf4",{"html":112,"metadata":113},"\u003Cp>Works on natural language processing and computational linguistics; she brings expertise in how language models handle shifting linguistic contexts, directly relevant to the workshop’s focus on evolving task definitions and evaluation criteria.\u003C/p>",{"headings":114,"localImagePaths":115,"remoteImagePaths":116,"frontmatter":117,"imagePaths":118},[],[],[],{"name":102,"affiliation":103,"talkTitle":16,"role":104,"url":105,"photo":106,"order":107},[],"rachel-bawden.md","papers",["Map",122,123],"paper-01",{"id":122,"data":124,"filePath":129,"digest":130,"rendered":131,"legacyId":140},{"title":125,"authors":126,"abstract":128,"order":86},"--paper-titile",[127,127,127],"Jane Smith","a long abstract","src/content/papers/paper-01.md","2a4e17610cfc1bf8",{"html":132,"metadata":133},"",{"headings":134,"localImagePaths":1