6,434,435],"dixon",{"id":339,"data":341,"body":347,"filePath":348,"digest":349,"rendered":350,"legacyId":358},{"name":342,"affiliation":343,"role":344,"title":345,"url":346,"order":86},"James Dixon","University of Oxford","volunteer","DPhil Student","https://eng.ox.ac.uk/about/machine-learning-research-group","DPhil (PhD) student at Oxford University MLRG, awarded a LASR studentship in recognition of his doctoral research proposal. His interests sits at the intersection of AI Security and mechanistic interpretability.","src/content/organisers/dixon.md","f740d3fa3b6a774e",{"html":351,"metadata":352},"\u003Cp>DPhil (PhD) student at Oxford University MLRG, awarded a LASR studentship in recognition of his doctoral research proposal. His interests sits at the intersection of AI Security and mechanistic interpretability.\u003C/p>",{"headings":353,"localImagePaths":354,"remoteImagePaths":355,"frontmatter":356,"imagePaths":357},[],[],[],{"name":342,"affiliation":343,"title":345,"url":346,"role":344,"order":86},[],"dixon.md","liu",{"id":359,"data":361,"body":367,"filePath":368,"digest":369,"rendered":370,"legacyId":378},{"name":362,"affiliation":363,"role":364,"title":62,"url":365,"photo":366,"order":65},"Fanghui Liu","University of Warwick","organiser","https://www.lfhsgre.org/","https://www.lfhsgre.org/images/me.jpg","Faculty member affiliated with the University of Warwick and Shanghai Jiao Tong University. His research studies the foundations of modern machine learning from the perspective of learning efficiency, nonlinearity, and post-training. He is a recipient of the AAAI New Faculty Award and Rising Stars in AI recognition. He was the main organizer of the [NeurIPS 2024 Fine-Tuning Workshop](https://sites.google.com/view/neurips2024-ftw/home).","src/content/organisers/liu.md","231b92fe07439a85",{"html":371,"metadata":372},"\u003Cp>Faculty member affiliated with the University of Warwick and Shanghai Jiao Tong University. His research studies the foundations of modern machine learning from the perspective of learning efficiency, nonlinearity, and post-training. He is a recipient of the AAAI New Faculty Award and Rising Stars in AI recognition. He was the main organizer of the \u003Ca href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/neurips2024-ftw/home\">NeurIPS 2024 Fine-Tuning Workshop\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>",{"headings":373,"localImagePaths":374,"remoteImagePaths":375,"frontmatter":376,"imagePaths":377},[],[],[],{"name":362,"affiliation":363,"title":62,"url":365,"role":364,"photo":366,"order":65},[],"liu.md","quinzan",{"id":379,"data":381,"body":386,"filePath":387,"digest":388,"rendered":389,"legacyId":397},{"name":382,"affiliation":343,"role":364,"title":383,"url":384,"photo":385,"order":86},"Francesco Quinzan","Senior Research Associate","https://sites.google.com/view/fquinz/home","https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/sitesv/AA5AbUBms_EOqCbEMyNa8D0EYl83DZrM8OsHmmZ6Tjcj5sl9MtYWnRQBWRUE-Yo2l0WE9IborA3EJXXIus9ypN0CJwRt2NkVZRuwR1cxvvDb-mCua9lPuBfkposoHq9aaQCnA9g29PU7wBNW_KpDUankdcehdiz49DqOH_jYn5L-K1LJ-RAxWg7EBa6nsywpTh22LiSapWUTbAEfA-qaGo2rgFrjRgB3ReoSPjUt3zgN0JE=w1280","Member of the Oxford Martin School, with an affiliated appointment at the University of Cambridge. His research lies at the intersection of AI safety, statistical learning, robustness, and alignment of foundation models. His work was recognized with various fellowships and competitive grants from UKRI, COST and other international programs. He organized the [2025 ML for Drug Discovery Workshop](https://mlfordd.com/) and the 2025 LLM@Oxford Workshop.","src/content/organisers/quinzan.md","ca5e72313fda9611",{"html":390,"metadata":391},"\u003Cp>Member of the Oxford Martin School, with an affiliated appointment at the University of Cambridge. His research lies at the intersection of AI safety, statistical learning, robustness, and alignment of foundation models. His work was recognized with various fellowships and competitive grants from UKRI, COST and other international programs. He organized the \u003Ca href=\"https://mlfordd.com/\">2025 ML for Drug Discovery Workshop\u003C/a> and the 2025 LLM@Oxford Workshop.\u003C/p>",{"headings":392,"localImagePaths":393,"remoteImagePaths":394,"frontmatter":395,"imagePaths":396},[],[],[],{"name":382,"affiliation":343,"title":383,"url":384,"role":364,"photo":385,"order":86},[],"quinzan.md","peyre",{"id":398,"data":400,"filePath":405,"digest":406,"rendered":407,"legacyId":414},{"name":401,"affiliation":402,"role":364,"title":403,"url":404,"order":21},"Gabriel Peyré","École Normale Supérieure","CNRS Research Director","https://www.gpeyre.com","src/content/organisers/peyre.md","eed3b04df2948811",{"html":132,"metadata":408},{"headings":409,"localImagePaths":410,"remoteImagePaths":411,"frontmatter":412,"imagePaths":413},[],[],[],{"name":401,"affiliation":402,"title":403,"url":404,"role":364,"order":21},[],"peyre.md","rebeschini",{"id":415,"data":417,"body":422,"filePath":423,"digest":424,"rendered":425,"legacyId":433},{"name":418,"affiliation":343,"role":364,"title":419,"url":420,"photo":421,"order":107},"Patrick Rebeschini","Full Professor","https://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/~rebeschi/","https://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/~rebeschi/images/bio/random.jpg","His research focuses on the statistical and theoretical foundations of machine learning, with particular emphasis on reinforcement learning, optimization, and implicit regularization. He is the recipient of an ERC Consolidator Grant and an Amazon Research Award. Patrick has organised numerous scientific events, including the Mathematics of Machine Learning Summer School at the [Alan Turing Institute](https://www.turing.ac.uk/). He is a Founding Member and current Director of the [Oxford ELLIS Unit](https://www.ellis.ox.ac.uk/).","src/content/organisers/rebeschini.md","62112f5356d66bc2",{"html":426,"metadata":427},"\u003Cp>His research focuses on the statistical and theoretical foundations of machine learning, with particular emphasis on reinforcement learning, optimization, and implicit regularization. He is the recipient of an ERC Consolidator Grant and an Amazon Research Award. Patrick has organised numerous scientific events, including the Mathematics of Machine Learning Summer School at the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.turing.ac.uk/\">Alan Turing Institute\u003C/a>. He is a Founding Member and current Director of the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.ellis.ox.ac.uk/\">Oxford ELLIS Unit\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>",{"headings":428,"localImagePaths":429,"remoteImagePaths":430,"frontmatter":431,"imagePaths":432},[],[],[],{"name":418,"affiliation":343,"title":419,"url":420,"role":364,"photo":421,"order":107},[],"rebeschini.md","shi",{"id":434,"data":436,"body":441,"filePath":442,"digest":443,"rendered":444,"legacyId":452},{"name":437,"affiliation":438,"role":364,"title":40,"url":439,"photo":440,"order":44},"Chengchun Shi","London School of Economics and Political Science","https://www.lse.ac.uk/people/chengchun-shi","https://callmespring.github.io/profile0.jpg","His research focuses on the statistical foundations of reinforcement learning, causal inference, and LLMs. Recipient of the Peter Gavin Hall IMS Early Career Prize, the IMS Tweedie Award, and the Royal Statistical Society Research Prize. Organiser of the [2026 Sanya Workshop on Causality and ML](https://tsimf.tsinghua.edu.cn/info/1107/1159.htm) and the [MLStat 2026 Conference](https://ml-stat.github.io/MLSTAT2026/).","src/content/organisers/shi.md","9d85ffa2fb33239d",{"html":445,"metadata":446},"\u003Cp>His research focuses on the statistical foundations of reinforcement learning, causal inference, and LLMs. Recipient of the Peter Gavin Hall IMS Early Career Prize, the IMS Tweedie Award, and the Royal Statistical Society Research Prize. Organiser of the \u003Ca href=\"https://tsimf.tsinghua.edu.cn/info/1107/1159.htm\">2026 Sanya Workshop on Causality and ML\u003C/a> and the \u003Ca href=\"https://ml-stat.github.io/MLSTAT2026/\">MLStat 2026 Conference\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>",{"headings":447,"localIm